# Line endings for the V13 prototypes, pinned per file.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The repo has core.autocrlf=true, which converts on
# checkout. These four files do NOT agree with each other on disk, and each is
# internally pure, so a blanket setting breaks half of them:
#
#   main dashboard.html          2122 CRLF, 0 bare LF
#   main-dashboard-states.html   1606 CRLF, 0 bare LF
#   positions screens.html          0 CRLF, 2931 LF
#   SESSION-2026-09-02.md           0 CRLF, 200 LF
#
# Without this file, a checkout would hand back "positions screens.html" as
# CRLF, and a blanket "-text" would hand back the two dashboards as LF. Both
# outcomes are silently wrong, and both matter: the agents editing these files
# patch by exact byte context and verify the ending counts afterwards, so a
# flipped file reads as corruption. A `sed -i` already converted one of these
# once, on 2026-09-02, and was caught only by that check.
#
# Patterns use `?` rather than quoting so the spaces in the filenames need no
# escaping. `?` matches exactly one character.
#
# If a file is ever deliberately converted, change its line here in the same
# commit, and re-measure rather than assuming.

positions*.html               text eol=lf
SESSION-*.md                  text eol=lf
main?dashboard.html           text eol=crlf
main-dashboard-states.html    text eol=crlf

# This file too, so the file that pins line endings is itself pinned.
.gitattributes                text eol=lf

# Reference screenshots, never diffed as text.
refs/**                       binary
*.png                         binary
